onsider the 未发货 prediction. Using SHIP planned_end + transit_p50 as pred, and err CDF by mode. But for orders whose SHIP node planned_end is already in the past and not done, that's captured by err>buffer naturally.\n\nBetter: for 未发货 orders, pred_receipt = max(SHIP planned_end, current open node planned_end + remaining node durations?) Let's check: is SHIP planned_end always the last node? sequence ordering: PLAN(1), PROCESS(2), ASSEMBLY(3), QC(4), SHIP(5) presumably. So SHIP planned_end is the last. Use SHIP planned_end as production-complete-and-dispatch plan.\n\nBut careful: for orders where SHIP node is already completed (actual_end not null) but shipment not received → that's the 在途 group.\n\nAlso for 未发货 orders, some may have no stage_nodes? All 769 effective have nodes (769 rows each for PLAN/QC/SHIP). Good.\n\nAdditional signal for 未发货: open procurement lines with supplier ETA later than promised receipt; QC failures; overdue nodes. Include as evidence.\n\nAlso should I incorporate \"node slip\" — i.e., if the current open node is already overdue (actual_end null and planned_end < now), the SHIP planned_end is likely optimistic. The err CDF by mode pools all orders regardless. A refinement: bucket err CDF by (mode, whether the order had overdue nodes at completion)? Too fancy. Instead: bucket by mode and use a \"delay-adjusted prediction\": pred_receipt = SHIP planned_end + max(0, days the current node is overdue) ... no, double counting.\n\nKeep it simple and documented: two-bucket model (mode-level err CDF), plus report node-overdue signals separately. Also report P90 receipt = pred + err_p90.\n\nLet me also compute P50/P90 of predicted receipt date: pred_receipt_p50 = SHIP_plan + transit_p50 + err_p50; p90 = + err_p90.\n\nLet me now check the err distribution quantiles by mode, and the transit quantiles by route. Then write the script.\n\nOne more consideration: min_samples=5 → if a bucket has <5 samples, fall back to a wider bucket and disclose.\n\nLet 